  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Novolacs&nbsp;are phenol-formaldehyde resins with a formaldehyde to phenol molar ratio of less than one.</p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0015_844d492c0634.png\" style=\"width: 487px; height: 280px;\" /></p><p>The rubber obtained is also&nbsp;called Styrene butadiene rubber (SBR). In Buna-S, Bu stands for butadiene and, Na for sodium and S for styrene. It is vulcanised with sulfur. The rubber is slightly inferior to natural rubber in its physical properties.</p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0015_36e03bfd76a0.png\" style=\"width: 379px; height: 140px;\" /></p><p>Glyptal- a polyester is formed by ethylene glycol and phthalic acid by step-growth polymerization.</p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0015_f4945ed88ac6.png\" style=\"width: 527px; height: 140px;\" /></p><p>Dacron obtained by condensation polymerisation of ethylene glycol and terephthalic acid at&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>420</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>460</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math>&nbsp;using zinc acetate and antimony oxide as catalyst.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0015_243fa91d2bc0.png\" style=\"width: 566px; height: 140px;\" /></p></blockquote>"
  }
